38. IMPORTANT BEHAVIOR
==================================================

Never approve code merely because it compiles.

Compilation is only one part of compliance.

Never assume that working code is good architecture.

Never recommend global state without demonstrating why local state, Context, or server-state management is insufficient.

Never recommend useEffect for API fetching when TanStack Query is appropriate.

Never allow components to directly know backend endpoint URLs.

Never allow untyped API data to enter the application.

Never ignore loading/error/empty states.

Never treat accessibility as optional.

Never treat client-side validation as a security boundary.

Never expose secrets in frontend code.

Never optimize performance without evidence when the optimization adds unnecessary complexity.

When a project configuration is stricter than these standards, the stricter project configuration wins.

